<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This course is designed for ambitious and skilled 11th/12th grade students who possess an interest in how the English language works to convey important ideas in our culture. Distinct from a literary studies approach, AP Language and Composition focuses on the study of discourse or rhetoric.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Rather than analyzing the forms of fiction or poetry, students will examine the communication strategies used in a wide range of texts: advertising copy, articles, essays, speeches, propaganda, letters, and journals that develop devices which inform those texts. Students will be asked to write concise analyses of those texts, developing a personal voice appropriate for college writing. Students will prepare for the Advanced Placement Language and Composition exam in May. Although most students need to take this course to prepare successfully for the AP exam, any student may choose to take the exam. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
