<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (AP Literature and Composition is an apt choice for 11th/12th graders who love to read closely and to write critically about literature \(story\). Students will read, discuss, and write about complex expressions of narrative art \(i.e., poetry, short stories, plays and novels\). Students are encouraged and expected to practice and develop their skills as active readers; much of this course aims to analyze closely the nuanced impact of authorial choices on meaning. This course will prepare students for the Advanced Placement exam in Literature and Composition given in May.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
