/S /P
/E (This course is the first in a three-year series of mathematics courses intended for students who have demonstrated a superior aptitude for, and interest in, the discipline of mathematics. The topics of instruction include both traditional Algebra II and Precalculus subjects. Among these are rational expressions, equations and inequalities, complex numbers, functions, conic sections, logarithms, systems, sequences, series, and probability. Heavy emphasis is placed on the development of college-level study habits, advanced critical thinking skills, and applications of all topics. A CAS TI-Nspire graphing calculator is highly recommended for all students in this course.)
