/E (This course covers topics of classical physics. Newtonian mechanics \(vector-based\), gravitation, conservation of energy, and momentum are covered in the first part of the course. The second part of the course covers electrostatics, DC circuits, waves, sound, light, and optics. Demonstrations and videos are used to supplement the lectures and to provide historical background for the laws of physics. Computer simulations, computerized data collection and analysis, and traditional hands-on lab activities are used throughout the course.)
