2311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This course explores the amazing and revolutionary discoveries made by astronomers about the cosmos. From our earliest ancestors to the present day, smart and creative people have made observations and built innovative instruments to better understand the universe we live in. This course will cover naked-eye astronomy, the constellations, the formation of the solar system, gravity and its effects on the planets, the nature of light and how telescopes work, the planets and other bodies in our solar system, and the newly-discovered solar systems beyond our own. This course is independent of Stellar Astronomy & Beyond and can be taken either before or after. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [14]
>>
