<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This course offers a study of people, places, and environments at the state, regional, national, and international level by examining both the physical and human geographical world. Using the essential elements of geography, students will learn content and skills that will help them navigate our society and a changing world. Additionally, this course will include geographic studies of world issues with connections to other social sciences including economics, political science, history, sociology, and anthropology.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [17]
